  "body_html": "<p>YugabyteDB is PostgreSQL compatible. It uses the same protocol and SQL layer as PostgreSQL. This makes YugabyteDB compatible with a majority of database tools, because PostgreSQL is the most popular open source database on the planet. Here is an example with Arctype, a user-friendly collaborative SQL client to query and visualize data.</p>\n\n<h2>Setting up a database connection</h2>\n\n<p>1. I went to <a href=\"https://arctype.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://arctype.com/</a> and downloaded the client for Windows.</p>\n\n<p>2. When I launched the app, I created an Arctype account and logged into it.</p>\n\n<p>3. At the Connect a Database step, I choose PostgreSQL and click Continue.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-Blog-Post-Image-8.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-Blog-Post-Image-8.png\" alt=\"Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>4. I enter my Host and Port info and click Continue.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-Blog-Post-Image-7.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-Blog-Post-Image-7.png\" alt=\"Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>5. I enter my database, username, password, and nickname for this database and click Continue.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 1\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>6. I enter my workspace name and click Continue.</p>\n\n<p>YugabyteDB is a distributed database. If you have a DNS entry with multiple IP addresses, you get high availability (in my tests, Arctype reconnects automatically).</p>\n\n<h2>Querying your database</h2>\n\n<p>I immediately can see the tables in my database, and query them. Some interesting features are variables – which runs prepared statements – and autocompletion from the catalog objects and the query aliases.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 2\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>You can visualize results on a grid (with search and export to .csv) or displayed as charts, like a heatmap.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 3\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>I can create tables from there, and also import a .csv.</p>\n\n<p>I’m imported a csv here (<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/komalkhetlani/coronavirus-covid19-vaccinations\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/komalkhetlani/coronavirus-covid19-vaccinations</a>). I used text, date and numeric datatypes.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 4\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>I can query and display in a grid…</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 5\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Or graphs that can be added to a dashboard…</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6.png\" class=\"article-body-image-wrapper\"><img src=\"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fblog.yugabyte.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2021%2F07%2FArctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 6\" width=\"800\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a></p>\n\n<p>All this is created in a workspace that can be shared with colleagues for team collaboration.</p>\n\n<p>This product is new, free to use, and has a community on Discord, to help. This is a nice way to get the power of SQL databases with a user-friendly interface. Of course, you can connect it to <a href=\"https://docs.yugabyte.com/latest/yugabyte-cloud/free-tier/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Yugabyte Cloud</a> and load various Open Data to learn the power of SQL.</p>\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n\n<p>We are here to help and answer any questions you may have. Join us on our <a href=\"https://www.yugabyte.com/slack\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">community Slack</a> channel, and star us on <a href=\"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub</a>.</p>\n\n",
  "body_markdown": "<p>YugabyteDB is PostgreSQL compatible. It uses the same protocol and SQL layer as PostgreSQL. This makes YugabyteDB compatible with a majority of database tools, because PostgreSQL is the most popular open source database on the planet. Here is an example with Arctype, a user-friendly collaborative SQL client to query and visualize data.</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left\">Setting up a database connection</h2>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">1. I went to <a href=\"https://arctype.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://arctype.com/</a> and downloaded the client for Windows.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">2. When I launched the app, I created an Arctype account and logged into it.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">3. At the Connect a Database step, I choose PostgreSQL and click Continue.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4445\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8.png\" alt=\"Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8.png 1999w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8-300x188.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8-1024x640.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8-768x480.png 768w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-8-1536x960.png 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1999px) 100vw, 1999px\" width=\"1999\" height=\"1250\"></p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">4. I enter my Host and Port info and click Continue.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4447\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7.png\" alt=\"Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7.png 1999w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7-300x188.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7-1024x640.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7-768x480.png 768w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-Blog-Post-Image-7-1536x960.png 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1999px) 100vw, 1999px\" width=\"1999\" height=\"1250\"></p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">5. I enter my database, username, password, and nickname for this database and click Continue.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4431\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 1\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1.png 1908w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1-300x164.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1-1024x558.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1-768x419.png 768w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-1-1536x837.png 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1908px) 100vw, 1908px\" width=\"1908\" height=\"1040\"></p>\n<p style=\"margin-left: 20px\">6. I enter my workspace name and click Continue.</p>\n<p>YugabyteDB is a distributed database. If you have a DNS entry with multiple IP addresses, you get high availability (in my tests, Arctype reconnects automatically).</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left\">Querying your database</h2>\n<p>I immediately can see the tables in my database, and query them. Some interesting features are variables – which runs prepared statements – and autocompletion from the catalog objects and the query aliases.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4432\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 2\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2.png 1324w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2-300x124.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2-1024x423.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-2-768x317.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1324px) 100vw, 1324px\" width=\"1324\" height=\"547\"></p>\n<p>You can visualize results on a grid (with search and export to .csv) or displayed as charts, like a heatmap.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4433\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 3\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3.png 1920w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3-300x155.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3-1024x529.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3-768x397.png 768w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-3-1536x794.png 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" width=\"1920\" height=\"992\"></p>\n<p>I can create tables from there, and also import a .csv.</p>\n<p>I’m imported a csv here (<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/komalkhetlani/coronavirus-covid19-vaccinations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.kaggle.com/komalkhetlani/coronavirus-covid19-vaccinations</a>). I used text, date and numeric datatypes.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4434\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 4\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4.png 1690w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4-300x173.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4-1024x589.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4-768x442.png 768w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-4-1536x883.png 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1690px) 100vw, 1690px\" width=\"1690\" height=\"972\"></p>\n<p>I can query and display in a grid…</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4435\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 5\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5.png 1113w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5-300x125.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5-1024x425.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-5-768x319.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1113px) 100vw, 1113px\" width=\"1113\" height=\"462\"></p>\n<p>Or graphs that can be added to a dashboard…</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-4436\" src=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6.png\" alt=\"Arctype + YB Blog Post Image 6\" srcset=\"https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6.png 1341w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6-300x117.png 300w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6-1024x400.png 1024w, https://blog.yugabyte.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Arctype-YB-Blog-Post-Image-6-768x300.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1341px) 100vw, 1341px\" width=\"1341\" height=\"524\"></p>\n<p>All this is created in a workspace that can be shared with colleagues for team collaboration.</p>\n<p>This product is new, free to use, and has a community on Discord, to help. This is a nice way to get the power of SQL databases with a user-friendly interface. Of course, you can connect it to <a href=\"https://docs.yugabyte.com/latest/yugabyte-cloud/free-tier/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Yugabyte Cloud</a>&nbsp;and load various Open Data to learn the power of SQL.</p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left\">Conclusion</h2>\n<p>We are here to help and answer any questions you may have. Join us on our <a href=\"https://www.yugabyte.com/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">community Slack</a>&nbsp;channel, and star us on&nbsp;<a href=\"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub</a>.</p>",
